{% doc %}
  Whether the current page is a programme page (DS-51): one on the programme template. Prints
  true or false; capture it and compare with 'true'.

  Until release, pages keep their old template names (L-08), and the new theme has none of them,
  so the seven programme pages fall back to the default page template. They are recognised here by
  those old names too, so the review theme lays them out as they will be after release.
  After release the release script moves them to the programme template: then delete the list.

  @example
  {%- capture programme_page -%}{% render 'gs-is-programme-page' %}{%- endcapture -%}
  {%- if programme_page contains 'true' -%} ... {%- endif -%}
{% enddoc %}
{%- liquid
  # The seven programme pages' template names before release (proposals/store-changes.md §3).
  assign old_names = 'artists-for-kids,the-smith-foundation,public-programs,speaker-series,music-at-the-smith,explore-create,art-in-good-company' | split: ','
  assign result = false
  if template.suffix == 'programme'
    assign result = true
  elsif page != blank and old_names contains page.template_suffix
    assign result = true
  endif
  echo result
-%}
